{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Step Back and Different Shades Of Blue feel like natural follow-ups because their guitar-driven blues connects with my recent interest in Clapton and Hendrix.",
    "In Session, Hot Rocks 1964-1971, and Frank Marino & Mahogany Rush - Live also connect with the blues-rooted playing I enjoy, even though I would save them for another visit."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Partners and The Very Best Of Paul Anka miss my current interest because vocal duets and traditional pop do not offer the blues guitar sound I want now.",
    "Time Out does not fit my current guitar-led blues mood, while Very Best Of and Greatest Hits leave me unable to judge a match without knowing the artists."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat an interest in established musicians as a reason to offer older music across styles, but that connection alone does not make me interested.",
    "Best-of collections seem to be treated as appealing next choices, although familiarity matters less to me than the particular artist and sound."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection I care about most right now is expressive blues guitar and roots rock, rather than simply music from a similar era.",
    "An album can fit my taste without being something I choose today: I would prioritize Step Back and Different Shades Of Blue and leave the other appealing options for later."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly capture my interest in blues-rooted guitar music but stretch it too broadly into older pop, jazz, and unspecified compilations."
}"}
